From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 01:21:55 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 05/12] LvglDisplayEngineDxe: Change passwords in dialogs

A password question is drawn as a text field whose text goes to the
browser as the new password. The text display engine does more
(PasswordProcess): it first checks whether the current password is
needed, by handing an empty one to PasswordCheck(), asks for it if so,
then asks for the new password twice. Drivers such as
UserAuthenticationDxe follow that sequence with a state machine: given
just the new password, they take it for the current one and the
password does not change.

Do the same here. A password question is a row with a "Change..."
button; ENTER or a click asks for the current password when one is set,
then for the new password and its confirmation, each in a modal dialog
with a field that shows bullets. Wrong current password, mismatch and
unsupported changes are reported in an alert, and the state machine of
the driver is reset when the user cancels. The dialogs run from the
event loop of the form, since LVGL does not run its timers from inside
an event handler. The text of a field is wiped when its dialog closes;
copies that LVGL leaves in freed memory while it grows the buffer as
the user types are not.

The alert loop of LvglHiiCreatePopup() becomes RunHiiPopup(), which the
password dialogs share, and the screen is redrawn as soon as a dialog
closes, before a driver may print its own messages.

